-- title:
--   k₀-level supersingular package: smooth charts, nodes, Drinfeld action
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $q$ be a prime with $5\le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. The curve data are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $=\kappa(j,\,j_{M'})$ over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the places in `ssPlaces q M' κ` (the places $w$ with `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ w`); the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$, into `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`; and a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, that is: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A\to\kappa$ on constants, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors under `Finsupp.mapDomain`, and the property that every nonzero element becomes, after scaling by a constant, an integral element with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is `coeffMap (IsLocalRing.residue ↥A) y`. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   **Hypotheses on the field of small constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element of $A$; the group `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` requires that $A\cap k_0$, formally `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, and with algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires that every $a\in A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and constants.** $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layers.** $\iota$ is a type, $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$ (`hAn`: $x\in A_n\iff x\in A$); $n_0$ is an index with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$ (`hn₀`); `hKcof` requires the family to be cofinal for finite sets: every finite subset of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$.
--
--   **Tame parameter and Galois stability.** $\pi_t\in\bar{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q$ and lies in $A$; `htame` requires every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$) with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` to fix $K_{n_0}$ pointwise, where `tameCharacter` is the residue of $\tau(\pi_t)/\pi_t$ when that quotient lies in $A$ and $0$ otherwise; `hk₀stab` requires every automorphism of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$ preserving $A$ setwise to preserve $k_0$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the following hold.
--
--   (C1) $F_0$ together with the constants generates everything: the join of `IntermediateField.adjoin ↥k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(fieldBar q M')))` and $F_0$ is $\top$.
--
--   (C2) $W_0$ cuts out $A$ on $k_0$: for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (C3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (C4) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (C5) There is $t\in W_0$ whose residue is transcendental in the following form: for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if `Polynomial.aeval t p` lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ lying in the maximal ideal.
--
--   (C6) Compatibility with the level-$M'$ constant reduction: let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$; assume $g$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which `jq` has non-negative order, and that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$. Then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that image and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (C7) Level equivariance: for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in$ `Gamma0 M'`, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ maps $F_0$ into itself, and for $f\in F_0$ with image in $F_0$, $f\in W_0$ if and only if its image is in $W_0$.
--
--   (C8) **Smooth-point half.** For every field `FSS` over $\kappa$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in `FSS` (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map to `FSS` with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A\to\kappa$ on constants, and the scaling property) such that $R.\mathrm{integers}$ cuts out $W_0$ on $F_0$, three things hold.
--
--   (C8a) *Drinfeld identification, fixed coefficient embedding.* For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ (`GaloisField q 2`), every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the action of $C_s$) with $\operatorname{card} C_s = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, such that for $\gamma\in$ `Gamma0 M'` with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the residual automorphism `R.resAut` of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` corresponds under $e$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) of that element.
--
--   (C8b) *Drinfeld identification with inertia.* For every ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbb F_{q^2}\to\kappa$, taken as the algebra structure, and every proof that the coordinate ring is a domain, there is one subgroup $C_s$ with $\operatorname{card} C_s = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for each $\zeta$ there is an isomorphism $e$ as in (C8a), satisfying the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance and in addition: for $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` and $\alpha\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $\iota(\alpha)=$ `A.tameCharacter πt τ`, and for $g$ the semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) (coefficientwise action of $\tau$), $g$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and for every ring automorphism $\varphi$ of `FSS` inducing the residual action of $g$, every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with image $\alpha^{q+1}$ in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$, and $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1},\alpha^q)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the map $e\circ\varphi$ agrees with `hFunctionFieldAction` of that element composed with $e$.
--
--   (C8c) *Ends, affine chart and layered smooth-point packages.* There are a finite set $N$ of places of `FSS` over $\kappa$ with $|N|=q+1$, and families $S_n(Q,n)$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, $\varphi_n(Q,n):\mathrm{Polynomial}\,A_n\to S_n(Q,n)$, $\chi_n(Q,n):S_n(Q,n)\to\kappa$ and sets $D_n(Q,n)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, indexed by places $Q$ of `FSS` and layers $n$, such that: there is a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` contained in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, contained in every $S_n(Q,n)$ with $Q\notin N$, and such that every $z\in$ `FSS` integral at all places outside $N$ is the $R$-residue of an element of $B$; and for each $Q\notin N$: for every layer $n$, the reduction $A_n\to\kappa$ is surjective, the constants from $A_n$ lie in $S_n(Q,n)$, $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified, $\varphi_n(Q,n)(\mathrm{C}\,a)$ is the constant $a$ and $\chi_n(Q,n)$ sends it to the residue of $a$, $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))=0$; for every $c\in A_n$ of residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_n(Q,n)\to A_n$ fixing the constants, compatible with $\chi_n(Q,n)$ on residues, and sending $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ to $c$; every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and its image in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_n(Q,n)$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ is $P$-integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and such that $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)=0$; every $\chi$ as above is realised by a unique $P\in D_n(Q,n)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f=\chi(f)$ for all $f$; on the subfield obtained by joining $F_0$ to the $k_0$-algebra generated by the image of $K_n$, membership in the valuation subring of $P\in D_n(Q,n)$ is equivalent to being a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in S_n(Q,n)$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h\ne0$; any nonzero element of that subfield of order $0$ at all $P\in D_n(Q,n)$ becomes a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant from $K_n$; any element of that subfield lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and integral at all $P\in D_n(Q,n)$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every element of $S_n(Q,n)$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ and the constants from $A_n$ and $h$ a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$. Moreover the rings $S_n(Q,n)$ increase with $K_n$, each $S_n(Q,n')$ lies in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ and the constants from $A_{n'}$ when $K_n\le K_{n'}$, the element $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ is independent of $n$, and the maps $\chi_n$ are compatible with the inclusions. Finally: a place $P$ lying in $D_n(Q,n)\cap D_n(Q',n)$ for $Q,Q'\notin N$ forces $Q=Q'$; every $P\in D_n(Q,n)$ has non-negative order on the image of `jq`; and for $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\bar{\mathbb Q}}($`fieldBar q M'`$)$ generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in$ `Gamma0 M'` and preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the set $N$ is stable under the induced action of `R.resAut τ`, and `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` $=D_n(\mathtt{R.resAut τ hτ • Q},n)$ for $Q\notin N$.
--
--   (C9) **Node half.** For every field `FSS` over $\kappa$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ as above with $R.\mathrm{integers}$ cutting out $W_0$ on $F_0$, there is a finite set $N$ of places of `FSS` over $\kappa$ with $|N|=q+1$, together with: fields $\mathrm{FIx}(x)$ over $\kappa$ indexed by places $x$, regular prolongations $\mathrm{Rx}(x)$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $\mathrm{FIx}(x)$ and places $\mathrm{bx}(x)$ of $\mathrm{FIx}(x)$; subrings $C'_l$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$; rings $\mathrm{Wc}_l$ which are complete discrete valuation domains with elements $\pi_l$, natural numbers $E_l$ and $E_0$; sets $S(\mathrm{nd})$ of places of `fieldBar q M'`, subrings $\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ and $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ of `fieldBar q M'` with $\mathcal N_0$ local and Noetherian, and elements $c_x,c_y,c_u$ indexed by places; subject to the following.
--
--   The constants: $C'_n = A\cap K_n$ (an element lies in $C'_n$ iff it lies in $A$ and in the image of $K_n$); an element of $C'_l$ has residue $0$ in $\kappa$ exactly when it is a multiple of $\varpi'_l$; $C'_{n_0}\le C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{n_0}\ne0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $1\le E_l$; every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with trivial tame character fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; and there are $w\ge1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}=v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$ in $A$.
--
--   For every $\mathrm{nd}\in N$: $\mathrm{bx}(\mathrm{nd})$, $\mathrm{nd}$ and all places in $S(\mathrm{nd})$ are rational; $\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ is the set of elements integral for $\mathrm{Rx}(\mathrm{nd})$, for $R$ and at every place of $S(\mathrm{nd})$, and such elements evaluate into $A$ at every place of $S(\mathrm{nd})$; $c_x c_y = (\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}c_u$ (constants transported to `fieldBar q M'`); $c_x$ has $\mathrm{Rx}$-residue $0$ while its $R$-residue has $\mathrm{nd}$-order $1$; $c_y$ has $R$-residue $0$ while its $\mathrm{Rx}$-residue has $\mathrm{bx}(\mathrm{nd})$-order $1$; for $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character and $g$ the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois` of $\tau$, the set $S(\mathrm{nd})$ is $g$-stable and $c_x,c_y$ are $g$-invariant; every element of `fieldBar q M'` is a quotient of elements of some $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$, and also becomes a finite $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)$ after multiplication by a nonzero element of that ring. For each layer $l$: $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)\le\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)\le\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$; a place $P$ belongs to $S(\mathrm{nd})$ exactly when $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ is $P$-integral and every nonunit of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ evaluates at $P$ into the maximal ideal of $A$; the constants from $C'_l$ lie in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$; every element of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ differs from a constant of $C'_l$ by a nonunit; a $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ with $C'_l$-linearly independent coefficients vanishes only if all those elements vanish; there is a subring $\mathrm{Bx}$ of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ containing $c_x,c_y,c_u$, with $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in\mathrm{Bx}$ and $h$ a unit of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$, and $\mathrm{Bx}$ generated by the constants of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x,c_y$ lie in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and $c_u$ is a unit of it; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $\mathrm{Wc}_l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ E l)` such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of the constant $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c\circ\sigma$ is the constant map `const (π l ^ E l)`, every constant of $C'_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and: an element $f$ of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ whose $\mathrm{Rx}$-residue is nonzero of $\mathrm{bx}(\mathrm{nd})$-order $n$ satisfies $\iota_c(f)\equiv\gamma V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by `const (π l ^ E l) (π l)` and $U$, for some unit $\gamma$; symmetrically, if its $R$-residue is nonzero of $\mathrm{nd}$-order $n$, then $\iota_c(f)\equiv\gamma U^n$ modulo the ideal generated by the same constant and $V$.
--
--   Further: distinct elements of $N$ have disjoint sets $S$; for $\mathrm{nd}\in N$ and $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$, every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-negative order wherever `jq` has, and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, evaluates at $P$ congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to every $a\in A$ whose residue is `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue; for each $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in$ `Gamma0 M'` there is a map $\tau_N$ on places preserving $N$ with $(\mathtt{levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ})\cdot P\in S(\mathrm{nd})\iff P\in S(\tau_N(\mathrm{nd}))$ and with $\mathrm{Rx}(\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $\mathrm{Rx}(\tau_N(\mathrm{nd})).\mathrm{integers}$; for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in$ `Gamma0 M'` and preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the place `R.resAut τ hτ • nd` lies in $N$ and `smulDisc τ (S nd)` $=S(\mathtt{R.resAut τ hτ • nd})$; for $\mathrm{nd}\in N$ the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $\mathrm{Rx}(\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$, and there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to $\mathrm{FIx}(\mathrm{nd})$ carrying $R_0$-residues to $\mathrm{Rx}(\mathrm{nd})$-residues and with $g$ integral at $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is integral at $\mathrm{bx}(\mathrm{nd})$.
--
--   The Hasse datum on the $q$-isogeny coordinate: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in `fieldBar q M'`, and there is $a_0\in A$ such that this element minus $a_0$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with residue $0$, while the residue of $a_0$ raised to the $q$-th power equals `s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')`; moreover there is a constant $c'$ with $c'\cdot(\mathtt{jqNModC}-a_0)$ in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero residue such that for every $\mathrm{nd}\in N$ the element $\mathtt{jqNModC}-a_0$ lies in $\mathrm{Rx}(\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue and $\mathrm{nd}.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $c'(\mathtt{jqNModC}-a_0)$ equals minus the $\mathrm{bx}(\mathrm{nd})$-order of that $\mathrm{Rx}$-residue.
--
--   Separation supplies: for $x\in N$ and any place $y\notin N$ there is $g$ in $R.\mathrm{integers}\cap\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$, a nonunit of $\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$, whose $R$-residue is nonzero of $y$-order $0$, and which is integral at every rational place of `fieldBar q M'` at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order; and for distinct $x,x'\in N$ there is $g$ which is $c_x(x)$ times a unit in $\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$ and a unit in $\mathcal N_0(x',n_0)$.
--
--   Finally, a covering statement: every rational place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` which specialises to $s$ — in the sense that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-negative order wherever `jq` has and with $R_0$-residue integral at $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue equals `s.evalAt` of that residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ — either lies in $S(\mathrm{nd})$ for some $\mathrm{nd}\in N$, or lies in a set $D$ for which there are a place $Q\notin N$ and an element $z$ with `R.IsResidueDisc Q D z`, i.e. $z$ is a disc coordinate for $D$ over $Q$ (all places of $D$ rational with $z$ integral of valuation $<1$, the $R$-residue of $z$ of $Q$-order $1$, a bijection between $D$ and the maximal ideal of $A$ by evaluation of $z$, order $1$ for $z$ minus its value, and a unit principle), together with the pointwise and degree compatibilities `R.PointwiseOn Q D` and `R.DegreeOn Q D`.
--
--   This is the $k_0$-level constructor for the stable model of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular place $s$ in characteristic $q$: it produces, over the small constant field $k_0$, a level field $F_0$ with a discrete valuation ring $W_0$, and then, for any regular prolongation of $A$ compatible with $W_0$, both halves of the local picture at $s$ — the $q+1$ smooth-point charts with their Drinfeld identification of the special fibre and its $\Gamma_0(M')$- and tame-inertia equivariance, and the $q+1$ nodes with their $uv$-crossing presentations, Igusa ends, Hasse datum on the $q$-isogeny coordinate, separation supplies and the covering of all places specialising to $s$. It is used by the supersingular regular-prolongation assembly that feeds the semistable covering of the full-level curve.
